# arenagen specification for pats_syntax.{sats,dats}: the level-0 AST (--compact)
# python3 ../utils/arenagen/arenagen.py --global sats pats_syntax.spec > pats_syntax_gen.hats
# python3 ../utils/arenagen/arenagen.py --global --compact dats pats_syntax.spec > pats_syntax_gen_dats.hats
#
# [record R (f: T, ..)] is an ATS1 record '{f= T, ..}: R_new(..), f(x) and x.f()
# [type N] with constructors is a datatype: N_CON(..), N_view (pattern matching)
# the typedef/vtypedef lines are copied to the .sats (after the abstypes)
# the names of the ATS1 fields and constructors are kept (D0Cextype of
# 3 arguments is renamed D0Cextype2); [List] is [glist], [Option] is [gopt]
